{
  "claim_limits": [
    "The 9 native structures, 27 stages, and 76 receipt chunks are counted per environment; the same 9 authored examples were repeated across 3 environments, not 27 independent designs.",
    "One four-neighbor material component establishes static contact, not physics, stability, structural strength, fluid flow, or actor traversal.",
    "Typed examples use the declared structural material scope; the arboretum has 1600 additional Seed cells outside that structural mask. Module compositions count all nonempty materials.",
    "Empty fraction counts every empty cell in the crop, including exterior space, unreachable voids, and unused margins; it is not a quality or traversability score.",
    "The six typed detail counts use before-detail versus after-detail native deltas because Metal is also primary structure and service material.",
    "Linux and Windows shader frames are not byte-identical; their exact native planes and bound palette source are identical. Renderer precision or color behavior was not separately isolated.",
    "Visual assessment was informed, nonblind specialist review. No owner acceptance, human preference trial, paid inference, model quality conclusion, or gameplay acceptance is implied.",
    "The viewport crop found after the first successful campaign is visibly corrected on Linux and Windows; physical owner mouse/keyboard, GPU, and gameplay acceptance remain separate.",
    "The small square-clearance exploration is a separate informed geometric review of explicit stage-level probe centers, not a frozen thirty-attempt metric or a new acceptance gate.",
    "This review qualifies the inspected artifacts and static architecture at the stated source; it does not supply Art conversation integration, authorized model inference, blind preference, physical stability, or complete gameplay levels."
